h to  become Captain America on top of that a  new organization is threatening the  world order the members call themselves  flag Smashers and they wish to restore  the world to its state before the blip  they obtain a serum similar to the one  given to Steve during World War II as  they find out there are more super  soldiers in the world including Isaiah  Bradley also an African-American who  helped the government during the Korean  war in the end Falcon and Bucky  succeeded in stopping the organization  and Sam accepts his role as the new  Captain America  especially when it comes to the cast  there is some interesting news for  example there are some actors from the  MCU that we are already familiar with  who will play in the film one returnee  is making it back into a Marvel  production for the first time in 16  years those who have already checked the  cast list we'll also have noticed that a  couple of names are missing who no  longer play a part in the story around  cap  but enough talk and let's get into the  details one thing that is already  certain is of course Anthony Mackey in  the role of Sam Wilson or from now on  better known as Captain America when the  movie premieres it'll be exactly 10  years and one month ago that Falcon  joined his friend Steve Rogers to  destroy Shield or rather Hydra we also  got to check out his suit in the last  episode of Falcon and the Winter Soldier  unlike Steve he naturally also has his  wingsuit at his disposal besides all the  white and red colors resemble even more  the flag of the United States  along with Mackie Danny Ramirez and Carl  Lumley are also back in the cast Ramirez  played the CIA agent Joaquin Torres who  already alerted Sam to the flag Smashers  in the series you'll most likely have a  similar role in the movie even if the  enemy organization is a lot more  powerful and dangerous with the New  World Order Carl Lumley AKA Isaiah  Bradley is also expected to reprise his  role the super soldier who is getting a  bit long in the tooth will surely no  longer actively intervened in the battle  but he will certainly help the young cap  with words and deeds new to the series  is Sabra whose real name is Ruth bad  saraf we may already see the young  Massad agent in secret Invasion as she  plays an important role in the  corresponding Comics the Asian  disembodied by the Israeli actress Shira  Haas who was last featured in the  miniseries unorthodox the fact that  Sabra is now being introduced in the MCU  is again a reason for many comic readers  to prick up their ears after all at  least in the comics not only is she an  agent but she's also a mutant after the  Cameo appearance of Charles Xavier in  Multiverse of Madness and the mentions  of mutations in Ms Marvel clues about  the X-Men and the MCU are becoming more  and more obvious  the bad guy is already part of the  film's title similar to Hydra it is  again not just a person but a whole  organization the eponymous new world  order this was founded early on by The  Red Skull and settled in the jungles of  the Amazon after years they tried to  manipulate the Hulk by brainwashing him  which they succeeded in doing for a  while however in the end Hulk Broke Free  from it and crushed the organization  along with the help of the Avengers  although they managed to reorganize a  short time later they were finally  destroyed by Apocalypse in the new movie  the organization is also joined by a  familiar face or rather a villain we  have not seen since the Incredible Hulk  we are talking about Dr Samuel Stearns  AKA leader as in the 2008 film he is  played by Tim Blake Nelson there he was  responsible for turning Emile Blonsky  into Hulk's enemy Abomination at the end  of the film he got some of Banner's  blood himself and its head began to  swell to this day Marvel has not  Incorporated this again fitting with  this announcement are also the rumors  about him being behind the attacks on  Jennifer Walters AKA She-Hulk in  addition to telepathic abilities leader  also has robots similar to Tony Stark  and Ultron in the comics which he built  himself and who fight on his side either  way we are very excited to see the new  old villain  unfortunately one character is no longer  part of the movie and this will surely  disappoint all fans of Falcon and the  Winter Soldier Sebastian Stan as Bucky  Barnes is sadly not featured in New  World Order especially the lack of  relationship between the two who are the  closest allies of Steve Rogers now  causes fans to feel more heartbroken yet  he has not gone from the franchise of  course while Sam fights alone against  leader Bucky plays an essential role in  the film Thunderbolts which will be  released shortly after not part of the  movie either will be Chris Evans as  Steve Rogers contrary to all rumors he  is stated via Twitter that there will  only be Sam  rumors of whether Emily Van Camp will be  back once again as Sharon Carter also  remained to be confirmed at the end of  the series spoiler alert it turns out  after all that she is the notorious  Crime Boss power broker it would be  appropriate that Sam is again dependent  on her help in some way when he once  again has to destroy an organization but  as mentioned nothing has been confirmed  nor denied so far  since the film is currently still in the  early stages of development there is not  that much information about the  production yet but there is a change of  director since the previous directors of  the Captain America movies namely Joe  and Anthony Russo are busy with other  Productions Julius Ona will take over  the nigerian-american filmmaker last  directed the drama loose which was  released in theaters in 2019 set to  return a scriptwriter and showrunner is  Malcolm Spellman he's the man who  previously wrote the story around Sam  Wilson on Falcon and the Winter Soldier  further information about the production  is sadly not available to us yet however  you can find all the futu